You don't believe that part?

241
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,263
[Jerry laughs]

242
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,808
-You think I said that for the camera.
-Yeah.

243
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:48,230
You remember ages ago, the, uh...
with the pollution warning.

244
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:51,275
Stay in your house and close the windows.

245
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:53,319
Oh, my God! I can't believe your memory.

246
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:56,697
Yeah. Correct me if I am wrong, 
but isn't the air inside the house...

247
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:58,949
doesn't it come from outside the house?

248
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,494
It's lovely. Lovely observation.

249
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:05,873
Pull that little plunger 
next to your eyeball vent out,

250
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:08,542
and you'll get air
coming through there, too. Pull that.

251
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:10,753
-What's an eyeball vent?
-That's the eyeball vent.

252
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:13,214
Is that what it's called?
Oh, 'cause it's like an eyeball.

253
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:15,883
-[Jerry] Right.
-'Cause it keeps your eyeballs cool.

254
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,886
"Uh, we need an eyeball vent."

255
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:20,638
"Why?" "I got hot eyeballs."

256
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:24,433
-[Mrs. Seinfeld] Hello?
-Hello!

257
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:26,310
[Mrs. Seinfeld] What's going on?

258
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:28,104
Uh, I'm sitting here with Ricky,

259
00:11:28,187 --> 00:11:30,398
and we're doing the show,
and we're in the car,

260
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:32,274
and there's been a huge accident.

261
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,693
[Mrs. Seinfeld] That's terrible.

262
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:37,363
We're in a $400,000 Rolls-Royce, though.

263
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:40,533
[Mrs. Seinfeld] Hopefully, comfortable.
Have you run out of things to talk about?

264
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:43,119
Are you asking have we run out of things 
to talk about,

265
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:46,372
or have we run out of things to talk about
and have stopped talking?

266
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:49,375
Because they're two different questions
with Jerry.

267
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:51,043
Yes, we've run out things to talk about,

268
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:53,170
-but we're still talking.
-[Jerry laughing]

269
00:11:58,342 --> 00:11:59,593
-Is that you?
-No.

270
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:01,846
-Your Dad?
-No.

271
00:12:03,597 --> 00:12:04,682
-Hitler?
-Yeah.

272
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:08,060
Can you believe I got it?
Where... I've never even seen that.

273
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,312
It's part of the show. I talk about...

274
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:15,317
about sci-fi, and I always go back
and kill Hitler.

275
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,695
And I go, I go,
"Well, people tried at the time,"

276
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,822
and they go, "No, I'd go back
and kill him as a baby."

277
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:23,075
I go, "You'd go back and find baby Hitler,
who hasn't done anything wrong yet,

278
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,368
and just strangle him?

279
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:25,494
Have you seen Hitler?"

280
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:28,497
And I pull this out of my pocket,
I go, "He was adorable!"

281
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:30,916
-And I show... And then, I...
-[both laughing]

282
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,212
How funny is it
that I guessed it in five?

283
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,299
-Is that saying something about you or me?
-Both of us.

284
00:12:38,382 --> 00:12:39,467
Yeah. [laughing]

285
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,509
[Jerry laughs]

286
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:50,478
And we have food.
We could've dive into that... fruit tart.

287
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,397
[laughs] Now, we're thinking
about surviving.

288
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:58,277
It's been 12 minutes, and we're already 
thinking about eating each other.

289
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,612
It's like... [laughing]

290
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:03,282
Look!

291
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,576
-[Jerry gasps]
-Oh, my God!

292
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,455
Wow! So quickly.

293
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:13,876
Oh, there it is, Ricky. 
Jesus! Look at that.

294
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:16,962
-Yeah, that's a big hit. That's a big hit.
-It flipped over.

295
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:20,508
They'll watch this, 
the person who's in that car.

296
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:23,385
-Oh, yeah.
-They'll watch this episode.

297
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:27,223
And they're in one of those full body
casts, but just the face showing.

298
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:28,349
[both laughing]

299
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:34,772
-[Ricky] Question.
-[Jerry] Yes, sir.

300
00:13:35,439 --> 00:13:38,108
Are you gonna leave in all that stuff
about the Chinese?

301
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:39,819
It's... No, I can't leave it in.

302
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:40,861
-Because...
-Oh!

303
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:44,240
Because... because it is
the worst kind of easy cliché.

304
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,033
But you can't help what you think.

305
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:48,619
-But you can help what you say.
-Exactly.

306
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:49,912
And I did.

307
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:50,829
[Jerry laughs]

308
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:52,206
[Ricky laughing]

309
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:07,096
Try and steal that. Try and break if off.

310
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:09,765
-Why would I do that?
-Try it. Just try and get it off.

311
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:11,976
Oh, is it, uh... is it a detachable thing?

312
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:15,020
Oh, does it go in when it's tampered with?

313
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:17,106
Yeah. But it's not working this morning.

314
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,107
[Ricky laughing]

315
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:24,405
-That's good. Do that again.
-I can't.

316
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:01,692
That's good that I can I can't.

